---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
import PhotoSlot from "../../components/PhotoSlot.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Where We Live"
  description="Where We Live — The Rare Renal Equity Project (REP): The Jentosy Project's initiative connecting geography, social determinants of health, and lived patient experience to kidney disease disparities."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Where We Live"
    heading="The Rare Renal Equity Project (REP)."
    lede="Place shapes kidney health as much as biology does. This initiative exists to make that visible — starting with the data we've already gathered on the Bronx."
  />

  <section class="on-light section-tight">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">What It Is</p>
      <h2 class="h3">Data, geography, and lived experience — together.</h2>
      <p>
        REP combines geographic data, social determinants of health, and patient storytelling to
        illustrate how place influences kidney health. Maps can identify neighborhoods with higher
        disease burden, fewer transplant referrals, or limited access to healthy food. Patient
        stories reveal what those conditions feel like day to day, and why the structural
        inequities behind them matter. Together, data and narrative build a fuller picture than
        either could alone.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="wide-image reveal">
      <PhotoSlot
        src="/images/WhereWeLiveThumbNail.webp"
        alt="A Where We Live — Rare Renal Equity Project community mapping session"
        ratio="16 / 9"
      />
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="on-light section-tight" style="border-top:1px solid var(--line);">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">What Exists Today</p>
      <h2 class="h3">The Bronx data behind this initiative.</h2>
      <p>
        The place-based numbers this initiative is built on already live on{" "}
        <a href="/the-need/data/">Bronx Data You Should Know</a> — Bronx population makeup, diabetes-hospitalization
        rates by race, and national CKD prevalence, sourced from the NY State Department of
        Health, CDC, and NIDDK. REP's job is to turn that data into geography a reader can
        actually see, not just read as a bar chart.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="on-dark section-tight">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">What's Next</p>
      <h2 class="h3" style="color:var(--ink-fg);">An interactive Bronx map — not built yet.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        The next stage of this initiative is a real, interactive map overlaying that
        disease-burden data onto Bronx neighborhood geography, paired with the patient stories
        that give the numbers context. It's an active initiative, not a finished product — support
        through partnership or funding directly moves this forward.
      </p>
      <div class="cluster gap-3" style="margin-top:var(--space-5);">
        <a href="/partner-with-us/" class="btn btn-steel-outline">Partner With Us</a>
        <a href="/donate/" class="btn btn-rust">Donate</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .wide-image {
    max-width: 620px;
    margin: var(--space-6) auto 0;
  }
</style>
